WEBVTT

00:01.290 --> 00:02.880
<i>You've probably heard of me.</i>

00:03.250 --> 00:04.630
<i>I'm Don Wei.</i>

00:05.380 --> 00:08.010
<i>Just when I thought I had
reached the peak of my career,</i>

00:08.380 --> 00:11.220
<i>I was handed the greatest challenge
ever faced by Man...</i>

00:11.890 --> 00:13.640
<i>to lead the Earth team
to victory</i>

00:13.810 --> 00:15.890
<i>in the Great Race of Oban.</i>

00:16.100 --> 00:17.810
<i>Since the start of the preselections</i>

00:18.020 --> 00:21.100
<i>on the planet Alwas,
we've had a few surprises.</i>

00:21.440 --> 00:23.610
<i>But I remain confident
we'll pull through.</i>

00:24.270 --> 00:26.030
<i>Winning, whatever the odds.</i>

00:26.190 --> 00:28.570
<i>That's what my job is all about.</i>

02:19.680 --> 02:21.430
Yeah! Way to go, Rick!

02:55.130 --> 02:56.300
Mommy!

03:15.990 --> 03:19.070
Now, listen up, everyone.
I've got good news and bad news.

03:19.240 --> 03:21.950
The good news is we've been
granted a rematch today.

03:22.740 --> 03:24.410
And the bad news is...

03:28.710 --> 03:30.170
Rick is out for at least a week.

03:31.420 --> 03:32.250
<i>No way.</i>

03:32.420 --> 03:34.050
We can't race without a pilot.

03:56.070 --> 03:58.450
May be I could
take his place?

03:58.610 --> 03:59.490
Jordan...

04:00.320 --> 04:01.990
Until further notice
you will be promoted

04:02.160 --> 04:04.700
to alternate pilot
for the Earth team.

04:05.450 --> 04:06.960
Me? But, sir, I...

04:09.960 --> 04:11.380
Come now, my boy,

04:11.540 --> 04:13.800
this is not the time
for false modesty.

04:13.960 --> 04:15.670
I know you'll do just fine.

04:19.760 --> 04:21.430
<i>This is not good.</i>

04:29.850 --> 04:32.900
Here it is, Jordan.
The Arrow 2, right out of the box.

04:33.060 --> 04:34.110
What do you think about it?

04:34.270 --> 04:36.690
Be gentle with it.
It's her first time.

04:36.860 --> 04:38.700
Hey, I guess that's true
for both of you!

04:45.700 --> 04:47.580
OK, Jordan, how about
a little practice?

04:47.750 --> 04:48.750
Ready?

04:49.460 --> 04:51.460
Let's start by warming up
the side reactors.

04:51.630 --> 04:52.540
You're doing fine.

04:52.710 --> 04:54.670
Remember, it's the green buttons
to your right.

04:57.670 --> 05:00.300
Your other right, Jordan.
Please concentrate.

05:24.620 --> 05:27.330
What are you doing?
Disengage the turbine accelerator!

05:28.080 --> 05:30.250
Help me! Get me out of here!

06:34.230 --> 06:36.020
Look, guys, I'm a gunner.

06:36.190 --> 06:38.690
I break things, it's my job.

06:38.900 --> 06:41.320
Don't worry. It was
a good attempt, Jordan, really.

06:41.820 --> 06:44.070
No, I've taken lessons.

06:44.280 --> 06:47.740
My first flying instructor
retired after teaching me.

06:49.450 --> 06:51.240
And now he works
with small animals.

06:56.830 --> 06:59.090
Stan, Koji.

06:59.630 --> 07:01.050
Don't even think about it.

07:01.210 --> 07:03.590
Koji and I are just
simple mechanics.

07:03.760 --> 07:05.510
We were never meant to fly.

07:08.760 --> 07:10.600
I'm sorry, sir.
We're just mechanics.

07:17.520 --> 07:19.400
I guess that just leaves me!

07:20.650 --> 07:22.860
I'm a great pilot, honest.

07:24.030 --> 07:25.570
Of course,
I've never really been

07:25.740 --> 07:27.610
behind the stick
of a real star-racer.

07:27.780 --> 07:30.780
But a machine is a machine
is a machine. Right, guys?

07:35.080 --> 07:37.330
I appreciate
your sense of duty, Molly,

07:37.500 --> 07:40.460
but I will never let an outsider,
let alone a girl,

07:40.590 --> 07:42.460
sacrifice herself for our team.

07:44.300 --> 07:46.010
You could at least try me out.

07:48.220 --> 07:50.680
I'll have to convince the judges
to give us a reprieve.

07:50.850 --> 07:52.060
It's the only way.

07:55.020 --> 07:58.100
We're coming with you.
Rick's accident was sabotage.

07:58.350 --> 08:00.190
I'm sure we can prove it to them.
Come on!

08:00.650 --> 08:02.230
Molly, keep an eye
on the pit while we're gone.

08:02.400 --> 08:03.650
And don't touch anything.

08:04.070 --> 08:06.110
Wait. I'm coming with you.

08:10.870 --> 08:11.870
Darn it!

08:26.260 --> 08:28.880
You know I saw
what happened yesterday.

08:30.300 --> 08:32.640
A real piece of bad luck.

08:33.260 --> 08:35.970
Guess you should have kept
those tarps on the ship.

08:38.020 --> 08:40.100
You have something on your mind?

08:40.270 --> 08:40.980
Bravo.

08:41.150 --> 08:43.860
And now can you guess
my birth sign, Sherlock?

08:44.480 --> 08:48.110
You know, ignoring your problems
is no way to solve them.

08:50.910 --> 08:54.240
Tell that to my dad.
He ignored me for ten years.

08:54.410 --> 08:57.790
Whose problem are we
talking about here, huh?

08:58.040 --> 09:00.620
Your problem, or your father's?

09:00.790 --> 09:02.880
Mind your own business!

09:07.630 --> 09:08.590
Hey, Pipsqueak.

09:09.470 --> 09:11.590
Come out in the open like a man.

09:23.060 --> 09:24.150
<i>Wow.</i>

09:34.740 --> 09:36.120
This could be a problem.

09:50.050 --> 09:53.550
But with a rocket seat,
it just might work.

09:54.050 --> 09:55.470
What a rotten bunch of...

09:56.510 --> 09:58.520
I'll show those slimy squids
what I'm made of.

09:58.680 --> 10:00.850
With all due respect, sir,
you should really think it over.

10:01.020 --> 10:03.940
I mean at your age
and without any prior training?

10:04.060 --> 10:07.270
I've been given a mission,
and I'll see it through like always.

10:07.770 --> 10:09.400
This really isn't happening.

10:09.860 --> 10:12.240
It's suicide, trust me.
I've been there.

10:15.320 --> 10:17.950
Sir, I think this is totally crazy.

10:18.120 --> 10:21.250
But for what it's worth,
I admire you. Even in death.

10:22.410 --> 10:24.080
-Thanks, Stan.
-Hey, look.

10:34.680 --> 10:35.390
Molly?

10:35.550 --> 10:37.970
Molly ! Set that ship down
immediately!

10:38.140 --> 10:40.640
Well don't just stand there.
Hold it to the ground.

10:40.810 --> 10:41.680
Yes, sir.

10:45.100 --> 10:47.230
Come on, now, baby.
Show me what you can do.

10:53.900 --> 10:55.110
Stop this ship!

10:55.740 --> 10:58.410
No, Jordan.
We can still win this race.

10:58.870 --> 11:00.450
What are you waiting for, Jordan?

11:01.700 --> 11:03.710
Are you with me,
or are you with me?

11:10.800 --> 11:11.840
Molly!

11:12.260 --> 11:14.220
Molly, this has gone far enough.

11:14.380 --> 11:17.340
-I order you to land that ship now!
-Don't worry. We'll be home early.

11:48.920 --> 11:51.130
Flint! Flint! Flint!

11:51.840 --> 11:54.670
Flint! Flint! Flint! Flint!

11:55.260 --> 11:57.430
The next race is a rematch.

11:57.590 --> 12:00.260
I now call forth Grooor!

12:06.890 --> 12:10.770
And now I call forth
the Earth team!

12:14.570 --> 12:16.530
The humans are so weak.

12:16.690 --> 12:19.660
They won't dare show
their face again.

12:37.300 --> 12:39.510
Pilot Molly reporting
for the Earth team.

12:43.140 --> 12:44.100
Molly?

12:44.260 --> 12:46.640
There's no Molly registered.

12:46.810 --> 12:49.020
She does appear
quite human, however.

12:49.190 --> 12:50.140
Then it's settled.

12:50.310 --> 12:52.860
Take your places
and let the race begin.

12:58.110 --> 12:58.950
Jordan.

12:59.740 --> 13:00.820
I'm counting on you.

13:01.110 --> 13:02.660
And you can count on me.

13:02.820 --> 13:04.280
"We can still win this race."

13:04.450 --> 13:05.740
What were you thinking, Jordan?

13:09.290 --> 13:10.290
Let's go.

13:13.080 --> 13:14.880
That's right, nice and easy.

13:15.670 --> 13:17.800
I think I'm getting
the hang of this.

13:22.550 --> 13:24.220
Please, don't let me be cloned.

13:48.910 --> 13:50.580
You poor fools.
You'll never make it.

13:55.380 --> 13:56.090
Easy.

13:56.840 --> 13:59.340
Why is the Arrow 2 so unstable?

13:59.510 --> 14:01.300
It appears that a rocket seat

14:01.470 --> 14:03.630
has been grafted
onto the steering column, sir.

14:03.800 --> 14:04.300
What?

14:10.060 --> 14:12.060
Fuselage OK at 85 percent.

14:14.770 --> 14:15.730
Eat this.

14:17.400 --> 14:18.610
It's my turn.

14:33.540 --> 14:35.250
Molly, do something.

14:37.290 --> 14:38.290
Here goes nothing.

14:48.640 --> 14:49.850
Where's that creep?

14:52.100 --> 14:53.770
Molly, your quaint control system

14:53.940 --> 14:56.150
is too simple for the Arrow 2.
Do you copy?

14:57.690 --> 15:00.780
We wouldn't be in this mess
if you had given me a trial run.

15:01.190 --> 15:02.740
Molly, listen!

15:02.860 --> 15:04.990
You are not the Earth team pilot.

15:07.490 --> 15:09.530
Molly, increase the thrust
of your side reactors.

15:09.950 --> 15:11.620
That should improve stability.

15:12.250 --> 15:13.620
Finally some good advice.

15:18.710 --> 15:19.710
Bingo!

15:22.000 --> 15:23.840
Koji, you're a genius.

15:24.470 --> 15:26.260
I'm only a humble mechanic.

15:29.510 --> 15:31.510
Come out,
you alien scum.

15:32.520 --> 15:33.890
He's right above us.

15:44.320 --> 15:45.950
It can't end like this.

15:46.400 --> 15:49.280
I could squash you
like an insect.

15:49.620 --> 15:53.620
But that would dishonor
all the insects of the Galaxy.

15:54.160 --> 15:57.540
Yesterday, you robbed Grooor
of a victory

15:57.710 --> 15:59.750
that was rightfully his.

16:00.130 --> 16:04.130
Today, your humiliation
must be complete.

16:08.590 --> 16:13.060
Grooor generously gives you
a lead of thirty seconds

16:13.310 --> 16:15.430
before your apocalypse.

16:18.850 --> 16:20.860
This is it.
This is our chance.

16:21.020 --> 16:22.110
I need more power.

16:22.570 --> 16:24.190
Power, power, power, power.

16:27.030 --> 16:27.950
Come on, baby.

16:28.860 --> 16:30.110
Just a little more.

16:34.580 --> 16:35.910
Now what's happening?

16:36.080 --> 16:37.580
Sir, the hyperdrive
has been engaged.

17:11.740 --> 17:12.740
Almost there.

17:20.870 --> 17:22.210
It's stopping.

17:22.630 --> 17:23.920
The plasma tanks are empty.

17:26.130 --> 17:27.300
The emergency batteries?

17:27.460 --> 17:30.010
Empty, sir.
The hyperdrive took everything.

17:30.170 --> 17:32.970
They may reach the finish line,
but they'll have to crawl.

17:39.480 --> 17:40.770
Grooor!

17:46.820 --> 17:47.780
Molly, Jordan!

17:48.110 --> 17:50.190
Abandon the Arrow 2
immediately!

17:50.440 --> 17:51.820
That's an order.

17:53.240 --> 17:53.860
<i>No way.</i>

17:55.370 --> 17:56.830
It's not over yet.

18:01.290 --> 18:02.580
Molly, what are you doing?

18:06.210 --> 18:07.340
Let's get out of here.

18:07.500 --> 18:09.670
Jordan, aim for the joints.

18:10.210 --> 18:11.720
Now, full power.

18:11.970 --> 18:12.550
Got it.

18:16.390 --> 18:18.600
Your lasers are worthless.

18:19.180 --> 18:21.100
You are mine.

18:28.610 --> 18:29.780
Grooor!

18:57.850 --> 18:59.100
<i>Groom“...</i>

19:03.060 --> 19:04.060
We're alive?

19:04.850 --> 19:06.190
We're alive! We're alive!

19:07.610 --> 19:08.940
Excellent!

19:42.810 --> 19:43.600
<i>We“...</i>

19:43.810 --> 19:45.810
You both should be
very proud of yourselves.

19:47.520 --> 19:50.400
Because I have never seen
a more terrible race

19:50.560 --> 19:52.270
in my entire career.

19:54.240 --> 19:56.900
You, Molly,
have disobeyed orders,

19:57.070 --> 19:58.820
damaged our last star-racer

19:59.200 --> 20:00.870
and needlessly risked your life,

20:01.030 --> 20:02.280
the life of your teammate,

20:02.450 --> 20:04.080
and the life of your manager.

20:04.500 --> 20:06.460
-But, but...
-But, but nothing.

20:07.080 --> 20:10.840
Jordan, your disobedience
is even more intolerable.

20:11.500 --> 20:13.050
Unlike your accomplice,

20:13.250 --> 20:15.210
you are an official member
of this team

20:15.340 --> 20:17.340
and a trained professional.

20:18.550 --> 20:19.550
Sorry.

20:20.300 --> 20:21.720
Sorry I let you down, sir.

20:22.640 --> 20:24.100
But this is ridiculous.

20:24.270 --> 20:26.930
We won the stupid race.
We won.

20:27.100 --> 20:30.310
You owe your victory
to a reckless stunt, young lady.

20:30.480 --> 20:34.110
Grooor was the better racer,
from beginning to end.

20:34.280 --> 20:37.490
We came
as ambassadors and now...

20:37.990 --> 20:41.660
we are the laughing stock
of the entire competition.

20:43.200 --> 20:45.200
Everyone, start packing.

20:45.910 --> 20:48.620
The Earth team is
withdrawing from the race.

20:57.170 --> 20:59.550
But we won the race.
We won!

21:07.980 --> 21:09.520
I'm so out of here!

21:12.310 --> 21:14.060
Molly, wait!

21:15.520 --> 21:18.990
Aw man, girls...
Way too sensitive.
